{
  "_meta": {
    "subsystem": "instruments_hvac_outlets",
    "source": "sheets 450 (24V outlets) + =07 700/710/720/730/740/750 (instruments) + =08 810/850/880/881 (ventilation & diesel air heaters) + =05 590/591 (monitoring/metering)",
    "voltage": 24,
    "note": "Combined batch. (1) 24V OUTLETS sheet 450 (PDF p53): one 15A fuse -F07 feeds three outlets (engine panel, nav station/coaming, USB at nav area shared with fridge sheet 570). (2) INSTRUMENTS =07 (PDF p88-93): two 25A feeds off MSB - -F16 ELECTRONICS via 24/24V 20A converter -U70, and -F15 AUTOPILOT direct - both onto the MSB_INSTR distribution bus; sub-fuses feed sailing instruments (B&G H5000/NMEA2000 via 24/12V conv -U720), navigation systems (B&G HALO24 radar, Zeus MFD x3, NEP2, forward-looking sonar FLS), communications (VHF/AIS via 24/12V conv -U740) and entertainment (Fusion via 24/12V conv -U750, plus instrument-light relay -K70). Foghorn (sheet 710) is on a separate FX04 feed. (3) VENTILATION/HEATERS =08: galley fan -MGF (via relay -K80, fuse -FX11), engine-room vent fans -M_ER1/-M_ER2 (-FX12), turbo fans -MT01..-MT05 (sheet 850, option 6080002), and TWO Webasto diesel air heaters - Air Top EVO 40 PORT (-HEATER_PT, fuse -FX06 15A + fuel pump -MFP_PT/-FX07 ctrl) and Air Top 2000 STC STBD (-HEATER_SB, fuse -FX08 15A + fuel pump -MFP_SB/-FX09 ctrl), both option 5080064, fed from the F90_POS direct bus. (4) MONITORING =05 (sheets 590/591, PDF p80-81): Blue Sea VSM 422 vessel system monitor + battery-volt check switch -S07, water/fuel metering fuse -FX02 5A and tank-monitor 24/12V converter -U1; tank-level senders themselves (fuel/water/blackwater Wema) belong to the tanks subsystem and are only referenced here. NOTE: sheets 860-865 'AIR CONDITION UNIT WEBASTO' are 230V AC (relays UC230V, L/N/PE) - they are NOT part of this 24V subsystem and were intentionally excluded (belong to AC 230V batch)."
  },
